<section id="nfsh" class="nfsh-article">
 <div class="nfsh-grid">
 
 <nav class="a-rail" aria-label="In this article">
 <p class="a-rail-h" data-t="rail_h">In this article</p>
 <ol data-nfsh-rail></ol>
 </nav>
 <div class="a-body">
 <p data-t="i1">The idea of our own footwear had been present at NORTHFINDER for years. The first samples were made more than ten years ago, but in the end they never reached the market. They were not yet what we wanted them to be.</p>
 <p data-t="i2">So we waited. For the right supplier, for experience, for development — and for the moment when we would know how to create footwear that would not be just another product in the collection.</p>
 <h2 id="nfsh-s1" data-nfsh-toc data-t="h2_1">Functional alone was not enough for us</h2>
 <p data-t="s1p1">The first NORTHFINDER shoe collections that did reach the market were already functional and well made, and customers took to them. Yet something was still missing — something that would make you say: <strong>this is NORTHFINDER</strong>.</p>
 <p data-t="s1p2">So when we developed the next generation, we did not start with the question of how the shoe should look. First we worked out who we are actually making it for, where they will wear it, what they need to handle in it and which properties should help them do that.</p>
 <p data-t="s1p3">Only then came the design.</p>
 <p data-t="s1p4">One of the first models in which this approach came through in full was the Nanda. Its development took roughly a year and a half to two years, and the result was meant to be a full-fledged technical hiking shoe that does not have to pretend colour has no place in the mountains.</p>
 <p data-t="s1p5">Outdoor footwear traditionally builds on safe colours — black, brown or grey. We decided to try another route.</p>
 <p data-t="s1p6">That is how the idea of <strong>Joyful meets performance</strong> came about: to combine uncompromising function, technical materials and the properties you need in the mountains with colours and a design you can simply enjoy.</p>
